# Monitoring stack secrets. Copy to .env; never commit the result.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# Or just run ./deploy.sh — it creates .env with a generated password on the
# first run and prints it once.

# Grafana admin password. Required — the compose file refuses to start without
# it, deliberately, so a stack is never brought up with a blank admin login.
GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UniFi polling is NOT part of this stack.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# unpoller was removed because the polling account has email MFA enforced, and
# unpoller authenticates with username/password against the controller login —
# which MFA blocks. UniFi data reaches the dashboard through the Network
# Integration API (an API key, set in the dashboard, not here) instead. See the
# project README section "UniFi with MFA" and the dashboard's Admin → API keys.
